%T A401357 185,169,221,185,193,205,229,221,233,313,293,325,277,317,289,305,305,
%U A401357 365,401,421,325,337,349,377,425,445,485,545,457,445,425,493,533,449,461,613,505,521,677
%N A401357 Hypotenuse of the unique primitive Pythagorean triangle whose legs sum to the n-th prime congruent to +-1 mod 8.
%C A401357 A prime p is the sum of the legs of a primitive Pythagorean triangle if and only if p == +-1 (mod 8), and then the triangle is unique (Wegener, Theorem 4.3; the uniqueness was also checked for the first 10000 terms). With legs m^2 - v^2 and 2*m*v, p = (m+v)^2 - 2*v^2 and the hypotenuse is m^2 + v^2.
%H A401357 Delano P. Wegener, <a href="https://www.fq.math.ca/Scanned/13-3/wegener.pdf">Primitive Pythagorean triples with sum or difference of legs equal to a prime</a>, Fibonacci Quarterly, Vol. 13, No. 3 (1975), pp. 263-277.
%F A401357 a(n) = (A002334(n+1) - A002335(n+1))^2 + A002335(n+1)^2. - _Alper Ferudun_, Oct 22 2026
%e A401357 a(1) = 5 because 7 = 3 + 4 and (3, 4, 5) is primitive; a(2) = 13 because 17 = 5 + 12.
%o A401357 (Python)
%o A401357 from sympy import primerange, gcd
%o A401357 from math import isqrt
%o A401357 def hyp(p):
%o A401357     for v in range(1, isqrt(p)+1):
%o A401357         s = p + 2*v*v; r = isqrt(s)
%o A401357         if r*r == s:
%o A401357             m = r - v
%o A401357             if m > v and gcd(m, v) == 1 and (m - v) % 2: return m*m + v*v
%o A401357 def A_list(N): return [hyp(p) for p in primerange(7, N) if p % 8 in (1, 7)]
%Y A401357 Cf. A001132, A002144, A002334, A002335.
%K A401357 nonn,new
%O A401357 1,1
%A A401357 _Pierre Colmant_, Oct 22 2026
